["If f'(x) is large in magnitude, the arc-length integrand √(1+(f')²) is generally:",["Larger","Zero","Exactly 1","Negative"],0,"A larger slope increases the length element."],
["The arc length of a curve is found by:",["Accumulating infinitesimal lengths","Adding y-values only","Finding the maximum","Differentiating twice"],0,"Integration accumulates the small length elements."],
["For a circle, arc length depends on:",["Radius and central angle","Only radius","Only area","Only diameter"],0,"For angle in radians, arc length is s=rθ."],
["A curve with greater bending may have a longer arc than the straight chord because:",["The curve path can exceed the direct distance","The chord is always longer","Area changes","The derivative is zero"],0,"A curved path between two points is generally at least as long as the straight chord."]
